			<div class="content" id="post-content-3776247">
									

<p>There's a rhyme and reason, here. A few notable details that might help:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>One of the people in the Cotter family picture has their face 'scratched out'. There's a reason.</li>
<li>The investigators mention a lot of things in their search of the Cotter house; the backyard, the sounds under the floorboards, the signs of extended habitation in the attic, the rancid smell&#8230; but there's one thing they don't mention. One part of the house we're told exists, but about which, no details are provided. <strong>ETA:</strong> I changed this to make it explicitly pointed out in the article (as I think it's a detail that was otherwise way too easy to miss).</li>
<li>Why did the Cotter family feel the need to 'plug up' all their faucets and drains with plaster?</li>
<li>The incident report mentions the house was demolished, but no evidence exists corroborating this.</li>
<li>During the search for the Bonafede family, two rescuers disappeared &#8212; and rather than keep looking, the sheriff moved the search elsewhere. The sheriff knows something.</li>
<li>D-BETA finds the initials 'A B' on the tree branch &#8212; who's initials are those? (Hint: One of the pictures tells you!)</li>
<li>It's mentioned that the house D-ALPHA comes across has a set of lights on in the attic.</li>
<li>Why was someone (or multiple someones) 'living in the trees' and not in the camp-site?</li>
<li>The doors to a set of stairs that the park ranger found in the woods? That was a <em>storm cellar</em>.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>(Not to imply that there's some deep, secret truth going on; just that a lot of the things going on in this skip are done for specific reasons, and meant to get you thinking about very specific possibilities)</p>

